# Tasks — GetYourRide Backend Build Plan (Tracking + Simulation)

This document covers **backend-only** work for GetYourRide_backend. Frontend/Android tracking UI is owned separately — see [`tasks-frontend.md`](tasks-frontend.md) for that scope, which is not part of this plan.

Each phase maps to a git branch, lists deliverables, specifies what gets checked/tested, and defines acceptance criteria before moving to the next phase.

> Backend repo: `kelvin-2/GetYourRide_backend`. Related docs: [`GetYourRide_Tracking_Documentation.md`](GetYourRide_Tracking_Documentation.md) for full API + architecture reference. For details on how Kiro's Spec workflow, steering files, hooks, and other IDE features work, see `docs/kiro-workflow.md` (create this alongside your steering files if it doesn't exist yet).

**Scope note:** as of this plan, there is no WebSocket/STOMP infrastructure on either side — Phase 3 below builds the backend's STOMP endpoint and message contracts only. Wiring an Android STOMP client to consume it is frontend work, tracked separately.

